{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The target argues that reliability comes from 'Social Error Correction' via inter-rater calibration, but it never addresses the problem's required distinction between a genuine reliability gain and mere checklist compliance that happens to track the right answer. If the panel's members independently apply the same checklist and converge, that is indistinguishable from mechanical compliance—the 'common language' could produce agreement that tracks the objective outcome without any genuine error-correction mechanism operating. The target offers no within-evaluation evidence to separate its hypothesized social correction from compliance; it asserts the mechanism but does not identify what observation would confirm it.","target":"97d404b52a17ddf6ccf8f2a6855fb6a70bc00c4a22d71a994af74e0e81de77c3"},{"attack":true,"case":"The target restricts its argument to 'open-world' tasks with latent variables not captured by the checklist, but the problem context fixes the task domain as 'tasks with objectively verifiable outcomes.' The proposed hidden-dependency failure mode is only a genuine objection if those hidden variables are themselves objectively verifiable but omitted from the checklist; if they are not objectively verifiable, they fall outside the problem's scope. The target never establishes that the latent variables it relies on are of the verifiable-but-omitted kind, so its central case against the panel may not apply to the problem as stated.","target":"bea325051be282f756fb7bed66468af34adc14338ef8ac68c2ad96287090482d"},{"attack":true,"case":"The 'Residual Error Divergence' criterion is unsound as a test of genuine reliability for non-experts. The problem specifies a panel of trained non-experts; the proposed evidence requires the panel to correctly override the checklist's literal output based on a 'gestalt' judgment of the totality of evidence. But a non-expert panel reliably recognizing when to override a checklist item that is misleading presupposes exactly the domain expertise the panel lacks. Thus the criterion either conflates the panel with experts or makes genuine reliability unattainable for the stated population, undermining its validity as a within-evaluation discriminator.","target":"db8d507ad2673d9f5d0782e85f1f2ce2e1722fa6c0038cbc937a587d778f1fed"},{"attack":false,"case":"","target":"fb03c276705355e50924c06a334bb3d9f3c453d50887dd40044180707517e747"}]}